3164-## What this skill does
3165-
3166:`spec.k` is a set of K reachability claims. `kprove` attempts to prove each claim by symbolically executing from the LHS and checking it reaches the RHS under the given conditions. When the proof fails, `kprove` exits non-zero and prints a residual configuration — the state it reached but could not close. This skill provides the tools to read that residual and extend `verification.k` until the proof closes.
3167-
3168-Use `writing-spec` before this skill if `spec.k` is not yet written.
--
3172-## Why proofs get stuck
3173-
3174:`kprove` closes a claim by rewriting the LHS to the RHS. It gets stuck when:
3175-
3176-- **Symbolic arithmetic does not reduce.** The backend cannot discharge the
--
3180-  configuration does not match the invariant claim's left-hand side closely
3181-  enough for the claim to apply, so the prover expands another iteration. See
3182:  [circularity debugging](../shared/kprove-debug-troubleshoot/circularity-not-applying.md).
3183-- **A helper rule is in the spec module instead of `verification.k`.** Plain `rule` statements in the spec module are a K compiler error; only `claim`s and `[simplification]` rules are allowed there.
